\section{MIEB-lite}
\label{sec:lite}
MIEB-lite is a 51-task subset that preserves diagnostic power at a fraction of the cost. We build it by pruning tasks with high inter-task correlation: iterative removal of tasks whose average correlation with others exceeds 0.5 (11 tasks) and then 0.45 (32 tasks). We then cluster the remaining tasks with UMAP and HDBSCAN~\cite{mcinnes2018umap,mcinnes2017hdbscan}, which yields 17 interpretable clusters, and keep representative tasks from each cluster so that category and difficulty coverage is preserved. Across 38 models, MIEB-lite agrees strongly with the full benchmark, with Spearman 0.992 and Pearson 0.986. For E5-V, the runtime drops from 264.0 to 46.4 H100 GPU hours, an 82.4\% reduction, as \autoref{tab: run time} shows.

